      "title": "Remove some unnecessary includes from header files",
      "message": "Remove some unnecessary includes from header files\n\nringbuffer.h hasn't needed to include wiretap/wtap.h for the\nlast 18 years (since e6886d90ce0ff33ee80acf3c2ea570333d8d5a23\nwhen pcapio was introduced), at least not for its own purposes.\n\nReplace that include with wireshark.h (so that we have stdbool),\nwhich is already included by wiretap/wtap.h\n\ncapture_opts.h has never needed ringbuffer.h, but it was accidentally\nadd in commit c14ea41233fa92a1cb97ef29d1f9ded6587e45a5. Remove it\nfrom the header. (capture_opts.c does, however, need it.)\n\nHowever, some other files did need some of the WTAP_ defines, and\ngot them through a chain of includes including ringbuffer.h. Add\nwiretap/wtap.h to those files.\n\n(A separate issue is that many files include wtap.h only for the\nvarious WTAP_ENCAP macros, and all files other than dumpcap only\nneed ringbuffer.h for macros like RINGBUFFER_MAX_NUM_FILES.)\n\nPing #19127\n",
